# Trellis — Windsurf Rules

You are working inside the **Trellis** monorepo — a personal knowledge graph platform.

Read `AGENTS.md` for the complete reference. Key points below.

## What You Can Do

- **Query the graph**: `just trellis query 'FIND calendaritem AS ?t WHERE ?t.type = "task"' --pretty`
- **CRUD entities**: `just trellis create/update/delete` — changes sync to the browser UI instantly via SSE
- **Manage ontologies**: `just trellis ontology create/update/delete` — auto-scaffolds UI (sidebar, browse page, dialog)
- **Link entities**: `just trellis link calendaritem:task-1 relatedTo calendaritem:note-1`
- **Watch mutations**: `just trellis watch --pretty`

## Architecture

```
apps/web/              Nuxt 3 app (localhost:4141)
packages/tql/          TQL kernel, EAV store, EQL-S query engine
packages/trellis-cli/  CLI + TypeScript SDK
packages/trellis-mcp/  MCP server (15 tools)
packages/types/        Shared TypeScript types
```

## Entity System

Two-axis: **class** (temporal, document, actor, container) × **type** (task, note, person, project, etc.)

Entity IDs: `calendaritem:task-1`, `calendaritem:note-meeting`

## Key Rules

- Dev server is always on `localhost:4141` — **never start it yourself**
- Pass `--agent-id cascade` to track your mutations
- Use descriptive entity ID slugs
- Mutations appear instantly in the browser via SSE
- Every entity needs at minimum `{ title: "..." }`

